{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hdm8YhhfuzTBkTpYLm5HNv","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, I found information about KIP-1312 (Support unregistering controllers) but the specific discussion details about the design decision on metadata record types are limited.\\\\n\\\\n## What I Found:\\\\n\\\\n**Final Design Decision: Introduce New Record Type**\\\\n\\\\nThe final implementation decision was to **introduce a new `UnregisterControllerRecord` metadata record type** rather than reuse an existing record type.\\\\n\\\\nThis is documented in:\\\\n- **`/store/pull-requests/22191.md`**: The PR implementing KIP-1312 explicitly states:\\\\n  > \\\\\\\"Introduce `UnregisterControllerRecord` metadata record schema + new MetadataVersion `IBP_4_4_IV2` to support this feature\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n- **`/store/WINDOW-108-2026-05-01-to-2026-05-02-summary.md`**: Confirms the same change:\\\\n  > \\\\\\\"Add controller-side handling and `UnregisterControllerRecord` metadata record\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n## Available Discussion Details:\\\\n\\\\nThe KIP-1312 discussion did include several follow-up questions from Jun Rao (documented in `/store/kips/KIP-1312.md` and `/store/WINDOW-107-2026-04-30-summary.md`):\\\\n- JR4: Use cases for `remove-controller` without `--unregister` flag\\\\n- JR5: Whether static quorums can have observer controllers  \\\\n- JR6: Wording clarifications\\\\n\\\\nHowever, **the specific debate about whether to reuse an existing record type versus introduce a new one does not appear to be captured in the available documentation**. The decision to use a dedicated `UnregisterControllerRecord` appears to have been established as part of the KIP's design rather than being a point of contention in the discussion threads I could access.\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1312.md\\\",\\\"WINDOW-108-2026-05-01-to-2026-05-02-summary.